1
00:00:00,002 --> 00:00:08,573
This is NetCoop AI: an evidence-seeking, multi-agent system that diagnoses network faults and explains why.

2
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:21,476
Built for the IIT Bhubaneswar Agentic AI challenge: specialist agents analyse telemetry, exchange structured findings, and agree on one evidence-backed diagnosis.

3
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:29,884
Network faults are distributed and ambiguous: a dead access point and a failed switch port can raise exactly the same alarms.

4
00:00:29,938 --> 00:00:40,498
NetCoop gives each domain its own agent, tests every explanation against the topology and timeline, and asks for missing evidence when two explanations tie.

5
00:00:40,552 --> 00:00:51,885
One investigation: validate the telemetry, analyse it in parallel, build competing hypotheses, request the deciding observation, then report.

6
00:00:51,940 --> 00:01:05,835
On 60 held-out synthetic scenarios, 59 had an acceptable outcome versus 22 for a threshold baseline. These are internally generated scenarios, not real-world accuracy.

7
00:01:05,886 --> 00:01:08,871
Let's open the Command Center.

8
00:01:08,924 --> 00:01:19,075
The sidebar holds navigation, a scenario launcher, and live status of the coordinator and the three specialist agents, each a separate process.

9
00:01:19,128 --> 00:01:27,269
We start with the organizer's own sample-generator data: a hardware failure on switch SW_CAMPUS_3.

10
00:01:27,321 --> 00:01:36,825
Run diagnosis creates an incident, ingests the records, and starts the three agents over the A2A protocol.

11
00:01:36,883 --> 00:01:46,109
The data source is labelled truthfully: organizer data from the problem statement's sample generator, mapped by a declared source profile.

12
00:01:46,164 --> 00:01:55,272
Fields the generator never defines, such as queue drops and status, are reported and not used. Nothing is guessed.

13
00:01:55,326 --> 00:02:02,365
This diagram is the heart of the system: the incident fans out to three specialists working in parallel.

14
00:02:02,421 --> 00:02:15,474
Performance found high latency and loss, Infrastructure found CPU at 99.9 percent, and Connectivity found nothing abnormal in its domain.

15
00:02:15,528 --> 00:02:23,373
Their findings flow into the STEaR reasoner. The evidence was decisive, so no verification was needed.

16
00:02:23,427 --> 00:02:33,615
Conclusion: device CPU overload at SW_CAMPUS_3, with moderate support, because all evidence comes from a single source.

17
00:02:33,669 --> 00:02:45,377
Confidence 0.88 is calibrated: conclusions of this kind were correct in 14 of 15 held-out cases. It is not a guessed percentage.

18
00:02:45,431 --> 00:02:54,729
The topology marks the faulted switch in red. The generator provides no topology, so this star layout is a labelled assumption.

19
00:02:54,784 --> 00:03:04,058
Below: the persisted timeline, the competing hypotheses with why the leader wins, and a plain summary with actions for an operator.

20
00:03:04,112 --> 00:03:12,382
Now evidence seeking: an access point is down, and the deciding data exists only in a wireless-controller archive.

21
00:03:12,436 --> 00:03:36,769
We run it, and all three agents start in parallel again.

22
00:03:36,823 --> 00:03:44,646
In round one STEaR was stuck: an access-point failure and a failed switch port predicted the same symptoms.

23
00:03:44,701 --> 00:03:54,591
Instead of guessing, it sent a targeted A2A verification task to the Infrastructure agent, asking only for the device status of AP-2-1.

24
00:03:54,645 --> 00:04:05,968
Twenty recorded observations came back, and round two concluded: device down at AP-2-1, high support, confidence 0.97.

25
00:04:06,022 --> 00:04:12,356
The topology now marks AP-2-1 as the root cause, with its impact scope highlighted.

26
00:04:12,416 --> 00:04:20,787
The specialists are discovered live over A2A, with their skills, metrics and loopback-only endpoints.

27
00:04:20,842 --> 00:04:31,350
Every exchange is persisted. Opening one shows the raw NDEP artifact exactly as the agent returned it, citing observation IDs.

28
00:04:31,402 --> 00:04:38,315
The reasoning page shows the decision basis, the ranking rule, and what changed round by round.

29
00:04:38,369 --> 00:04:48,193
Every hypothesis is listed as confirmed, plausible, or ruled out by observed evidence, with its contradictions and missing discriminators.

30
00:04:48,247 --> 00:04:55,506
The Evidence Explorer shows validated observations with explicit units, freshness and quality flags.

31
00:04:55,559 --> 00:05:03,025
Each one traces back to the immutable raw record it came from, so every number in a report is auditable.

32
00:05:03,078 --> 00:05:11,938
Datasets and Upload accepts NDEP JSON, vendor CSV through declared profiles, and the organizer's format.

33
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:24,845
This organizer scenario has deliberately corrupted records: a renamed field with the wrong unit, a missing device ID, a bad timestamp, an impossible value and a duplicate.

34
00:05:24,899 --> 00:05:35,307
Each problem is reported record by record and never silently coerced. The diagnosis continues on the valid data and honestly reports an unknown fault.

35
00:05:35,361 --> 00:05:48,236
The report is the schema-validated JSON the problem statement asks for: cause, evidence, affected devices, alternatives, confidence, actions and limitations.

36
00:05:48,290 --> 00:05:54,666
Limitations are stated in every report, including the scope of the confidence calibration.

37
00:05:54,720 --> 00:06:01,295
The same report can be viewed as JSON and exported; a text version is available too.

38
00:06:01,349 --> 00:06:11,727
Evaluation compares four methods on the held-out set, with the caveats first: synthetic data, same authors, not root-cause accuracy.

39
00:06:11,781 --> 00:06:21,504
Full NetCoop has the most acceptable outcomes and no high-support mistakes; verification is what turns ambiguous cases into identified ones.

40
00:06:21,558 --> 00:06:29,466
Settings shows the backend connection and readiness. A clearly labelled recorded preview works even without a backend.

41
00:06:29,521 --> 00:06:41,745
Everything runs locally with one command, start.sh or start.ps1 on Windows. A verified release ZIP and a single-container Render image are included.

42
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:53,606
No LLM is required: the diagnosis is deterministic and tested, and every claim links to real evidence. Thank you for watching.
